// Title: Potential Binary Proxy Execution Via VSDiagnostics.EXE
// Sigma ID: ac1c92b4-ac81-405a-9978-4604d78cc47e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects execution of "VSDiagnostics.exe" with the "start" command in order to launch and proxy
//   arbitrary binaries.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage for tracing and diagnostics purposes
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/0xBoku/status/1679200664013135872
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_vsdiagnostics_execution_proxy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\VSDiagnostics.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "VSDiagnostics.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "start" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /launch:" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -launch:")
